            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Kissing&quot; stents for bifurcational coronary lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coronary stents implantation into each vessel of a bifurcational lesion (&quot;kissing&quot; stents) in two patients is reported. The first patient had two short &quot;kissing&quot; stents implanted in an ostial lesion of the left anterior descending and the intermediate branch. The second patient had successful &quot;kissing&quot; stents implantation in the bifurcational lesion of the left main coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
